/*
 * Declares the TemplateRefMethodValue class.

 * TemplateRefMethodValue represents a reference to a method template in the
 * generator IR. It specializes TemplateRefValue for the case where the template
 * denotes a class method rather than a free function or constructor. These
 * references appear during name resolution when an identifier refers to a
 * method template, typically in expressions such as `obj.method` or qualified
 * template accesses.
 *
 * The class stores both the template symbol and the class symbol to which the
 * method belongs. It provides access to the method’s syntax declaration, its
 * name, and mutability information derived from the prototype.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::template::method
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/template/method.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-11-20
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
